# aurora.local / packages/notes/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/notes/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here. Copy or merge into packages/notes/pins.env to adopt.
#
# See dev/notes/pinnable-versions-progress.md for the full inventory and
# reasoning behind every choice in this file.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run.
# compose.yml is untouched by this work.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>

# ghcr.io/silverbulletmd/silverbullet — this is the exact image the task
# brief calls out as today's problem case (`:latest`). Latest stable
# release is 2.10.0, published 2026-07-28 (~18 days before this check,
# past the fortnight bar, not marked pre-release). Multi-arch: linux/amd64,
# linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64 — confirmed via `docker buildx imagetools
# inspect`; covers both the Optiplex (amd64) and a Pi (arm64). Note:
# `:latest` currently resolves to a *different* digest than `2.10.0` —
# most likely a base-image security rebuild rather than a new app version
# (no newer numbered release was found), but it means `:latest` has
# already drifted from the tagged release in the short time since
# 2.10.0 shipped, which is itself the argument for pinning to the
# version tag rather than chasing `:latest`. Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_SILVERBULLET=ghcr.io/silverbulletmd/silverbullet:2.10.0@sha256:27b5724cc36798e7de82180ec9898ea9c157c4f15127f279834bca2897b91f37
